	    // and if the return value is true, new list's index of x is either >= old list's index of x or equals -1.  If return value is false, new list's count is equal to old list's count
        } 
    }
}

```

Also, this test method checks if the return value is based on the new list's last index of "x". If the returned value is true, it checks that new list's last index of "x" is greater than or equal to the old list's last index of "x". If the return value is true, it also checks that new list's index of "x" is either greater than or equal to the old list's index of "x" or remains at -1. If the return value is false, it verifies that the new list's count is equal to the old list's count. 

For more detail on how to use PexObserve and Debug.Assert, please refer to the documentation here:

[PexObserve](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/dn907259.aspx)

[Debug.Assert](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/zd3924kc.aspx)

