## Conclusion
This blog has explained how to write a code coverage test with NUnit and Pex tool in Visual Studio 2017 and how to interpret the code coverage results. It also described how to write a code coverage test for .NET collections (ArrayList class) using Pex. Writing a meaningful code coverage test ensures the software behaves as expected, and it detects potential bugs and vulnerabilities in real-time, which further reduces the possibility of introducing errors during the development and maintenance process.

