How can I also modify the back button text dynamically in the same way?
Many thanks in advance.

A: Unfortunately, the Ionic v4 does not provide any direct method to change the back button text. The framework treats the Back Button as a browser back button on which the text can be changed only through specific configurations in the user's browser settings.
If you are looking forward to change the back button on dynamically, you may want to override the whole back button or make use of custom buttons or components for your pages, where you can fully customize the back behavior as well as visual appearance.

A: It appears that there is a lack of support for changing the back button title in Ionic v4 for now. The back button title change is more suitable in browser and you control the title from the browser's settings, not on the application side.
As per my knowledge, this is available in NavigationExtras as you've commented earlier, but as of now, it's not supported in Ionic v4.
You have to handle the change in Back Button title by the platform your application runs on.
For iOS, it's handled by the browser but for Android, it's primarily handled by the application.
For any future updates or changes in Ionic, it would be best to keep an eye on their official Angular forums or on their Github Repo.
And as a work around, you could use a custom back button which you manually control.

A: For me, Ionic v4.7.2 and angular 7, it is possible to change back button text dynamically.
You need to set the title on navigateForward dynamically by creating an object with title:
this.navCtrl.navigateForward('YourPage', {
    title: "Your Title"
});

Then, you need to--------------------	    Assert.True(New_Ret == true ? New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX : true, "If return value is true, new list's last index of x is >= old list's last index of x");

